# GENERATED by herwig7/production/make_cards.py from herwig7/DIS-nu-PWGNEG.in -- edit the generator, not this file.
# v2 production (PRODUCTION.md): FASER ladder nu neg target p
#   E_lab = 2000 GeV, k.P = E_lab * 0.938272 GeV2, beams (c.m.) = [30.627634, 30.642003] GeV
#   target beam p+, PDF NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180
#   region faser; generation cuts: Q2 > 4.0 GeV2, NO y cut (Miny 0 / Maxy 1 on BOTH cut objects),
#   LeptonicCut MinW2 0.3 GeV2 -- deliberately LOOSER than the region, see
#   make_cards.py.  The exact Q2 > 4, W > 3 GeV is applied in the analysis.
#   Comments below that
#   mention 0.2 < y < 0.9, p+ or 1 TeV describe the template.
# NEGATIVE half of the NLO cross section -- run alongside DIS-nu-POWHEG.in.
#
# Herwig's DISBase splits the NLO weight into its positive and negative parts
# and generates them as two SEPARATE positive-weight samples:
#     Contribution 1  "PositiveNLO"  ->  max(0,  w)
#     Contribution 2  "NegativeNLO"  ->  max(0, -w)
# (MatrixElement/DIS/DISBase.cc::NLOWeight, and the Contribution switch in
# DISBase.cc::Init).  Herwig's own defaults set Contribution 1 on
# PowhegMEDISNC/CC, so a single run out of the box delivers ONLY the positive
# half -- it is not the NLO cross section.  The physical result is
#     sigma_NLO = sigma(Contribution 1) - sigma(Contribution 2)
# and likewise for any distribution or channel rate.
#
# This card is DIS-nu-POWHEG.in with that one switch flipped.
# -*- ThePEG-repository -*-
##############################################################################
# LO CC neutrino DIS for the FASER evgen benchmark (Herwig 7.3.0)
#
# nu_mu p -> mu- X, run in the nu-p c.m. frame like the Sherpa benchmark:
# beams [nu_mu, p+] with E = [21.654469, 21.674786] GeV (sqrt(s) = 43.32926),
# the EXACT c.m. energies of a massless 1 TeV nu_mu on a proton at rest, so
# 2 k.P = 1876.5440 GeV^2; the analysis is frame-invariant.
#
# CC counterpart of DIS-mu.in -- identical except for the beam (nu_mu), the
# matrix element (MEDISCC instead of MEDISNC) and the cut object
# (ChargedCurrentCut instead of NeutralCurrentCut).
#
# Conventions matched:
#  - LO MEDISCC (t-channel W), O(alphas^0)
#  - proton PDF NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180 via LHAPDF (hard ME + backward shower)
#  - muF = Q for the hard ME (DISBase default: scale = -tHat = Q2)
#  - fixed alpha_em = 1/132.119, sin2thetaW = 0.22291 via EW/Scheme Independent
#  - generation cuts = fiducial cuts: Q2 > 4 GeV2, 0.2 < y < 0.9
#  - default angular-ordered shower + cluster hadronisation; MPI off
#  - stable-particle convention ctau > 10 mm
#
# usage: Herwig read DIS-nu-POL.in ; Herwig run DIS-nu-POL.run -N NEV -s SEED
##############################################################################

read snippets/EPCollider.in

##################################################
# beams: nu_mu (A, +z) on p+ (B, -z), nu-p c.m. frame
##################################################
cd /Herwig/EventHandlers
set EventHandler:BeamA /Herwig/Particles/nu_mu
set Luminosity:BeamEMaxA 30.627634*GeV
set EventHandler:BeamB /Herwig/Particles/p+
set Luminosity:BeamEMaxB 30.642003*GeV

##################################################
# proton PDF: NNPDF4.0 NNLO via LHAPDF
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Partons
create ThePEG::LHAPDF NNPDF40 ThePEGLHAPDF.so
set NNPDF40:PDFName NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180
set NNPDF40:RemnantHandler HadronRemnants
set /Herwig/Particles/p+:PDF NNPDF40
set EPExtractor:SecondPDF NNPDF40
set /Herwig/Shower/ShowerHandler:PDFB NNPDF40

##################################################
# EW parameters: fixed alpha_em = 1/132.119,
# sin2thetaW = 0.22291 (Gmu-matched benchmark values).
# For CC the whole normalisation is (alpha/sin2thetaW)^2 / (Q2+m_W^2)^2,
# i.e. G_F^2 m_W^4; see NEUTRINO_NOTES.md for the 0.2% G_F convention spread.
##################################################
cd /Herwig
set Model:EW/Scheme Independent
set Model:EW/AlphaEMMZ 0.007568934067015342
set Model:EW/Sin2ThetaW 0.22291

##################################################
# hard process: LO charged-current DIS (t-channel W)
##################################################
cd /Herwig/MatrixElements
# POWHEG NLO charged-current DIS.  PowhegMEDISCC is created in Herwig's
# defaults as Herwig::MEChargedCurrentDIS with Contribution 1 -- i.e. the SAME
# class as the LO matrix element -- so it takes the code path in which the
# polarized-beam branch below is honoured.  Matchbox does NOT: its CC Born came
# out at 0.4935 of the analytic value, the neutrino factor 2, and declaring a
# left-handed beam had no effect on it.
insert SubProcess:MatrixElements[0] PowhegMEDISCC
set PowhegMEDISCC:Contribution 2
cd /Herwig/Shower
set ShowerHandler:HardEmission POWHEG
cd /Herwig/MatrixElements
# (superseded: this card IS now the POWHEG route)
# NOTE: PowhegMEDISCC exists in Herwig 7.3.0 -- the natural route to an
# NLO-matched Herwig CC neutrino sample (Contribution 1 + PowhegShowerHandler)

##################################################
# generation cuts = fiducial region
##################################################
# TRAP: SimpleDISCut defaults are MinQ2 = 20 GeV2 AND MaxQ2 = 100 GeV2 for
# ChargedCurrentCut -- both silently wrong for this benchmark
# LEPTONIC CUT, generation cuts == fiducial cuts.  Both lessons from the muon
# NLO strand: a parton-based y cut breaks the IR cancellation at NLO, and
# generating WIDER than fiducial makes sigma_fid = sigma_gen x (weight
# fraction) blow up because the out-of-fiducial slices carry net negative
# weight.  With the cuts coincident, sigma_fid IS sigma_gen.
library LeptonicDISCut.so
create ThePEG::LeptonicDISCut /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:MinQ2 4.0*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:MaxQ2 1000000.0*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:Miny 0.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:Maxy 1.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:MinW2 0.3*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut:ChargedCurrent Yes
insert /Herwig/Cuts/Cuts:TwoCuts[0] /Herwig/Cuts/LeptonicCut

set /Herwig/Cuts/ChargedCurrentCut:MinQ2 4.0*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/ChargedCurrentCut:MaxQ2 1000000.0*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/ChargedCurrentCut:Miny 0.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/ChargedCurrentCut:Maxy 1.0

##################################################
# no QED radiation in the shower: lepton splittings are
# already removed by EPCollider.in; remove the quark ones
##################################################
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting u->u,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting d->d,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting s->s,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting c->c,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting b->b,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting t->t,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting u->u,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting d->d,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting s->s,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting c->c,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting b->b,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting t->t,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting d->gamma,d; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting u->gamma,u; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting s->gamma,s; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting c->gamma,c; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do /Herwig/Shower/SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting b->gamma,b; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov

##################################################
# stable-particle convention: ctau > 10 mm stable
##################################################
set /Herwig/Decays/DecayHandler:MaxLifeTime 10*mm
set /Herwig/Decays/DecayHandler:LifeTimeOption Average

##################################################
# HepMC3 Ascii output
##################################################
##################################################
# POLARIZED NEUTRINO BEAM
# ThePEG's nu_mu is a plain BeamParticleData, so MEChargedCurrentDIS
# falls through to the unconditional  me *= 0.25  (1/2 lepton x 1/2 quark
# spin average) -- wrong for a massless neutrino, which has one helicity.
# Declaring the beam as PolarizedBeamParticleData with
# LongitudinalPolarization = -1 (rho = diag(1,0), pure left-handed) makes
# the ME use  menew.average(rho_lepton, rho_quark)  instead.
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Particles
create ThePEG::PolarizedBeamParticleData nu_mu_L
setup nu_mu_L 14 nu_mu 0 0.  0 0 0 0 2 1
create ThePEG::PolarizedBeamParticleData nu_mubar_L
setup nu_mubar_L -14 nu_mubar 0 0.  0 0 0 0 2 1
makeanti nu_mubar_L nu_mu_L
set nu_mu_L:LongitudinalPolarization -1.0
set nu_mubar_L:LongitudinalPolarization 1.0
cd /Herwig/EventHandlers
set EventHandler:BeamA /Herwig/Particles/nu_mu_L
# ESSENTIAL: the ME's mePartonData() comes from the DIAGRAM, built with
# getParticleData(14) -- i.e. the generator's particle map, not the beam
# object.  Setting BeamA alone therefore has NO effect (verified: bit-identical
# cross-section).  LocalParticles overrides the id-14 entry of that map.
insert /Herwig/Generators/EventGenerator:LocalParticles 0 /Herwig/Particles/nu_mu_L
insert /Herwig/Generators/EventGenerator:LocalParticles 0 /Herwig/Particles/nu_mubar_L

read snippets/HepMC.in
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Format GenEventHepMC3
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Filename events.hepmc
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:PrintEvent 100000000
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Units GeV_mm

##################################################
# generator settings
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Generators
set EventGenerator:MaxErrors 10000
##################################################
# INTRINSIC pT: 0.5 GeV, NOT Herwig's default 2.2
##################################################
# Herwig's default IntrinsicPtGaussian is 2.2 GeV, a value tuned to LHC data.
# This benchmark runs at sqrt(s) = 43 GeV, and there 2.2 GeV of transverse
# momentum handed to the beam remnant is a large fraction of the transverse
# scale available: the shower's momentum reconstruction then fails, and Herwig
# DISCARDS the event -- "Failed to generate the shower after 100 attempts in
# ShowerHandler::cascade()".
#
# MEASURED, and it is not a small effect (2026-09-01).  With the POWHEG
# hardest emission on, the default discards 5.9% of generated muon events
# against 1.1% with the emission off; the discards are NOT a random subset --
# losing them raises <Q2> by 2.8%, so they sit at the bottom of the Q2 range.
# herwig_xsec.py then restores the rate from the integrated cross-section,
# which is correct for the total and spreads the missing low-Q2 events over
# every bin.  The visible symptoms were a Q2 spectrum tilted from -5% to +8%
# across the range at Q2 > 4, and a flat +3.7% excess at Q2 > 11.
#
#     IntrinsicPtGaussian   survival   <Q2>     sigma/YADISM (Q2 > 11)
#     2.2 GeV (default)      0.9396    15.561        1.0368
#     0.5 GeV (here)         0.9808    15.023        0.9874
#     0.0 GeV                0.9516    14.871          --
#
# 0.5 GeV rather than 0: zero is NOT the best value -- it survives worse
# (0.9516) and undershoots <Q2> -- and a few hundred MeV of intrinsic
# transverse momentum is what fixed-target DIS tunes carry anyway.  This is a
# non-perturbative parameter that MUST be set for the beam energy in use;
# carrying an LHC value to a 43 GeV collision is the bug, not the fix.
set /Herwig/Shower/ShowerHandler:IntrinsicPtGaussian 0.5*GeV

# v2: a failed remnant/shower is rebuilt on the SAME phase-space
# point, never replaced by a new one (make_cards.py RETRIES)
set /Herwig/EventHandlers/EventHandler:MaxEventErrorRetries 100
# v2: never move the scattered lepton to rescue the remnant; the
# event fails and is retried instead (make_cards.py RETRIES)
set /Herwig/Partons/RemnantDecayer:DISRemnantOption NoLepton
saverun FL-nu-PWGNEG-p-2TeV EventGenerator
